# Context Metrics and Removal — measure, remove, evaluate

Status: **active** — C1 and C2 are built and exercised; C3 is the next slice.

Implements the intent-network measurement family (../intent-network/04-sidecar,
05-evaluation-layer, 08-context-mechanisms) inside the manage plugin +
state.db. Supersedes doc 18's S4 (digests + prune — the compacting half is
C2) and S6 (skill tiers — reduced to machine tags), and doc 10 (skills
gating — reduced to capture plus optional validation). Wording/injection is
deliberately not the mechanism: intent is measured, not prompted.

## As built

| Piece | State |
|---|---|
| C1 capture (turn_metrics, context_events) | live — verified: 32 turns, 44 tool calls, 8 proposals recorded in one session store |
| C1 read (`:ManageMetrics`, `metrics.turns/events`) | live — colon-call driver fix required first |
| C2 prune request + shaped compaction | live — requests and consumes recorded; compaction effect confirmed via token columns on following turns |
| C2 interface (`<leader>at`, `:ManagePrune`) | built — persistent two-pane viewer over turns + per-turn event windows |
| C3 evaluation | pending |

Two driver bugs had to die first, both silent: the lsqlite3-style API
(`db:exec`/`db:prepare`) does not exist in kkharji/sqlite.lua, and
`sqlite.open(path)` (dot-call) passes no self — sqlite.lua then falls back to
an in-memory DB. Both fixed; the store now persists for nvim and plugin
alike. Plugin-side, `node:sqlite` does not exist under Bun — the shared
lib/sqlite.ts loader picks `bun:sqlite` or `node:sqlite` at runtime.

## The problem

Context only grows. Every turn adds tool output, dead ends, superseded code,
and plan text; nothing removes any of it. Removal must be structural and its
effect measurable, or it is theater.

## Architecture

```
session events ──► manage.ts hooks ──► state.db (turn_metrics, context_events, verdicts)
                                              │
                    nvim console ◄────────────┤  :ManageMetrics · <leader>at
                                              │
nvim :ManagePrune ──► prune_request row ──► plugin claims on next message
                                              │
                     experimental.session.compacting shapes ──► client.session.summarize
```

- Capture is plugin-only (event + tool hooks). No new process.
- Storage is the existing `state.db` (project + global), additive tables.
- Removal reads metrics + verdicts; it never asks the model to decide.

## C1 — Measure (built)

| Table | Row per | Columns |
|---|---|---|
| turn_metrics | assistant message (upsert by message_id) | session_id, message_id, ts, tokens_input/output/reasoning, cache_read/write, model, agent |
| context_events | notable act | session_id, ts, kind (tool_call / skill_load / proposal / registry_proposal / prune_request / prune_consumed), detail, subject |

Capture points: `message.updated` (assistant usage), `tool.execute.after`
(tool calls), `tool.execute.before` on `skill` (skill loads), proposal and
registry emits. Reads: `:ManageMetrics` (one-shot) and `<leader>at` (viewer,
below). Aggregation views: `v_session_growth`, `v_tool_usage`.

Skills policy manifest (tags only) remains optional and unbuilt; when it
exists, `context_events.subject` attributes skill loads.

## C2 — Remove (built, coarse first)

The flow, as implemented:

1. In nvim: `:ManagePrune [note]` — writes one `prune_request` event into
   `context_events`. No side effects on opencode until claimed.
2. On the next user message, the plugin claims the request (newest request
   newer than newest consume): `prune_consumed` row + in-memory flag.
3. `experimental.session.compacting` then shapes that compaction: keep
   verified state, accepted/rejected outcomes, decisions, changed paths,
   open questions, the current task; drop exploration, superseded code and
   plans, tool noise.
4. `client.session.summarize({ path: { id } })` triggers the compaction. On
   failure the request is kept and retried on the next message (log:
   `[manage] prune: summarize failed`).

Acceptance: `cache_read` / `tokens_input` in `turn_metrics` shrink on the
turns following a prune; the viewer shows request → consume directly.

Honest limit: this pass compacts the whole session with keep/drop
instructions — coarse. Selective removal (rewriting old message ranges via
`messages.transform`) is the finer pass, deliberately later.

## Interface

- `<leader>at` — metrics viewer: turns list (time · in · out · cache),
  detail pane shows the selected turn's metadata plus every context event in
  its window (between the previous turn and this one), winbar shows totals
  and prune status. Keys: `j/k`, `r`, `Q`.
- `:ManageMetrics` — one-shot summary in `:messages`.
- `:ManagePrune [note]` — request a prune.
- Errors and driver messages: `:messages` (verdicts/metrics notify at ERROR
  level; there is no silent fail-open in the nvim store anymore).

## C3 — Evaluate (pending)

Derived stats from verdicts + turn_metrics (SQL, no model): per-path
verdict counts and recency; per-group acceptance rate; per-prune
effectiveness (did corrections on pruned content follow). Feeds retention
tiers (intent-network 08 section 3). Explainable stats only; mechanism
promotion/demotion (05) later.

## Honest limits

- Compaction verification: the summarize call returns success; whether the
  visible compaction ran is confirmed by the following turns' token columns
  and the TUI's compaction marker.
- Token metrics depend on provider usage fields; absent fields are skipped.
- Removal is structural first: verified slices, verdict history, recency.
- Continuous verdict capture (every user message, not just proposal
  completions) with origin weights — proposal outcomes high-confidence,
  conversation signals review-gated — is the queued follow-up in the
  intent-network verdict docs (10/11), not this doc.

## Slices

| Slice | Content | State |
|---|---|---|
| **C1** | metrics capture + read interface | done |
| **C2** | prune request + shaped compaction | done (coarse) |
| **C3** | verdict-derived stats + retention candidates | next |

## Open questions

1. Prune trigger: manual only for now; token-threshold automatic comes only
   after C3 shows the stats.
2. Protected window: last N turns untouched — relevant to the selective
   (messages.transform) pass.
3. Selective removal pass: when C2's measured effect justifies the risk.

